(3156634, 440344, 31637, '<td valign="top">this is just brilliant !</td>', 'this is just brilliant !', '2006-12-28 15:44:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3156851, 438821, 30454, '<td valign="top">Wow, what a wonderful shot. Congrates on your first ribbon. Your porfolio is really impressive.</td>', 'Wow, what a wonderful shot. Congrates on your first ribbon. Your porfolio is really impressive.', '2006-12-28 16:57:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3156890, 440344, 30454, '<td valign="top">I am always amazed with all of your this kind of shots. Congrates on the well deserved Blue ribbon.</td>', 'I am always amazed with all of your this kind of shots. Congrates on the well deserved Blue ribbon.', '2006-12-28 17:11:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3157239, 440344, 60964, '<td valign="top">Thats really cool.  One drop is bouncing up the other is coming down and they crash in the air.  I just spent quite a bit of time trying to recreate this shot, its really hard to catch it in the right moment.  I think i need a drop dispensing machine.</td>', 'Thats really cool.  One drop is bouncing up the other is coming down and they crash in the air.  I just spent quite a bit of time trying to recreate this shot, its really hard to catch it in the right moment.  I think i need a drop dispensing machine.', '2006-12-28 19:22:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3157629, 439585, 31606, '<td valign="top">Beings you want to enter challenges and learn from that I chose this image to comment on.  First your image is very small as I am sure you got tons of comments on.  I amnot sure what you are editing with but this might help: <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26</a> <br/> <br/>Also remember this is an art site.  So you need to seek out interesting perspectives and stuff that shows off the beauty of your subject, beauty is found in everything.  Even if it is just a barn take the time to walk around it, get low, get high, try different angles and see what you can come up with.</td>', 'Beings you want to enter challenges and learn from that I chose this image to comment on.  First your image is very small as I am sure you got tons of comments on.  I amnot sure what you are editing with but this might help: //www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26  Also remember this is an art site.  So you need to seek out interesting perspectives and stuff that shows off the beauty of your subject, beauty is found in everything.  Even if it is just a barn take the time to walk around it, get low, get high, try different angles and see what you can come up with.', '2006-12-28 22:25:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3157689, 439961, 61818, '<td valign="top">I like this shot a lot.  Too bad about the DQ.  Look forward to seeing more of your work!</td>', 'I like this shot a lot.  Too bad about the DQ.  Look forward to seeing more of your work!', '2006-12-28 22:50:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3157824, 440043, 50641, '<td valign="top">Yes, you did get the saturation just right.   I don''t understand why the cruddy 4 and below votes.  I didn''t vote in brown but perhaps like the sticky challenge, the topic put voters in a lousy mood. However, you got a nice full histogram with lots of high votes too :) The focus on your leaf is so nice.  Maybe they didn''t like the blur on the right?  I guess that could be creatively cropped but it really changes the composition.  Gutteral?  Ha! Ach! Ich haben a laugh over that, you Deutscher you ;-)</td>', 'Yes, you did get the saturation just right.   I don''t understand why the cruddy 4 and below votes.  I didn''t vote in brown but perhaps like the sticky challenge, the topic put voters in a lousy mood. However, you got a nice full histogram with lots of high votes too :) The focus on your leaf is so nice.  Maybe they didn''t like the blur on the right?  I guess that could be creatively cropped but it really changes the composition.  Gutteral?  Ha! Ach! Ich haben a laugh over that, you Deutscher you ;-)', '2006-12-28 23:24:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3158242, 440042, 50641, '<td valign="top">I like the composition  - particularly the angle of the shoes. It''s very nifty the way the mirror completes the scene for us.  Gentle lighting - keeps it nice and warm. My favorite part is the grain of the wood floor.  Would have gotten a good vote from me!</td>', 'I like the composition  - particularly the angle of the shoes. It''s very nifty the way the mirror completes the scene for us.  Gentle lighting - keeps it nice and warm. My favorite part is the grain of the wood floor.  Would have gotten a good vote from me!', '2006-12-29 01:22:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3158318, 440368, 50641, '<td valign="top">Excellent mix of textures!</td>', 'Excellent mix of textures!', '2006-12-29 01:42:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3158409, 439562, 50641, '<td valign="top">Agree with noraneko about the photo filters - they can give things a nice nudge.  I''m really loving the skinny warped-looking trees to the left.  These voters will usually require a more pronounced subject unfortunately.  However, this shot might be fun for applying a filter or an effect.  If you have PS - try liquify to give the warpy trees an even bigger wobble. Perhaps glowing outlines. Actually, with all this nice contrast, you might try a simple b/w or duotone conversion.  If all else fails, make a composite  - add an image....  giant gerbil maybe?  :)</td>', 'Agree with noraneko about the photo filters - they can give things a nice nudge.  I''m really loving the skinny warped-looking trees to the left.  These voters will usually require a more pronounced subject unfortunately.  However, this shot might be fun for applying a filter or an effect.  If you have PS - try liquify to give the warpy trees an even bigger wobble. Perhaps glowing outlines. Actually, with all this nice contrast, you might try a simple b/w or duotone conversion.  If all else fails, make a composite  - add an image....  giant gerbil maybe?  :)', '2006-12-29 02:18:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3158751, 440324, 39165, '<td valign="top">I love this image! any chance for a ''step-by-step'' type thing for us noobs? :)</td>', 'I love this image! any chance for a ''step-by-step'' type thing for us noobs? :)', '2006-12-29 07:34:49.000000', NULL, 0),
