(3160580, 440324, 20608, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by snackwells:</b></div><hr/><i> While this is an exceptional photograph, unless I''m mistaken, tone mapping in Photomatix is not considered legal under basic rules. Yes? No? Maybe? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It is legal if you use tonemapping on a single JPG and apply it to the whole image, and this has already been validated. Thank you<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-29 21:20:41.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by snackwells: While this is an exceptional photograph, unless I''m mistaken, tone mapping in Photomatix is not considered legal under basic rules. Yes? No? Maybe?   It is legal if you use tonemapping on a single JPG and apply it to the whole image, and this has already been validated. Thank you', '2006-12-29 18:40:25.000000', '2006-12-29 21:20:41.000000', 0),
