(3167277, 440344, 52549, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by legalbeagle:</b></div><hr/><i> Looks like you''ve been dugg!  Lots more comments here...<br/> <br/><a href="//www.digg.com/design/great_image_of_a_coffee_with_a_drop_of_milk_highspeed" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.digg.com/design/great_image_of_a_coffee_with_a_drop_of_milk_highspeed</a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi Matthew,<br/>My first instinct is to join that site and get into the fray of things on the thread ;-) To tell some of them how wrong they are in their assumptions: It is not a stopped video clip, there are no backdrops, mirrors, umbrellas, no sound/photogate triggers etc.....and to tell them I''m not a "poor girl" because I use a Tamron 90 mm macro ;-)) But I won''t...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-01-02 11:16:21.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by legalbeagle: Looks like you''ve been dugg!  Lots more comments here... //www.digg.com/design/great_image_of_a_coffee_with_a_drop_of_milk_highspeed   Hi Matthew,My first instinct is to join that site and get into the fray of things on the thread ;-) To tell some of them how wrong they are in their assumptions: It is not a stopped video clip, there are no backdrops, mirrors, umbrellas, no sound/photogate triggers etc.....and to tell them I''m not a "poor girl" because I use a Tamron 90 mm macro ;-)) But I won''t...', '2007-01-01 10:15:09.000000', '2007-01-02 11:16:21.000000', 0),
